### Statement of Changes (GPL-2.0 §2(a))

This distribution has been modified relative to the upstream. The complete,
detailed change list is in [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) and
[`docs/OUR-CHANGES.md`](docs/OUR-CHANGES.md). Summary:

1. `entry/src/main/ets/pages/Index.ets` — `startBg()` no longer calls
   `requestBgStop()` first; the `16000068` (ability already exists) branch now
   re-delivers the want via `startAbility(want)` without options after 300 ms
   instead of logging and returning.
2. `entry/src/main/ets/background/BackGroundAbility.ets` — added `onNewWant()`
   so a running carrier ability accepts a new `host` parameter. Upstream did not
   implement it.
3. `entry/src/main/ets/background/BackGroundAbility.ets` — added `doConnect()`,
   which retries up to 10 times at 600 ms intervals when the native layer
   returns "previous client is still stopping, please retry in a moment".
4. `entry/src/main/ets/net/ServerDiscovery.ets` and
   `entry/src/main/ets/background/BackGroundAbility.ets` — added
   `DISCOVERY_PORT_BG = 47001`, a `listenPort` parameter on
   `startServerDiscovery()`, and `watchBeacon()` for server-IP change self-healing.
5. `entry/src/main/cpp/protocol/deskflow_client.cpp` — the `AUTHORIZING` branch
   now cancels and re-requests injection authorization; added
   `recoverInjectionPermission()` with rate limiting (>= 5000 ms apart, <= 8
   total), wired into the four `inject*` failure branches.

### Documented limitations

No clipboard synchronization is provided. Reading the clipboard requires
`ohos.permission.READ_PASTEBOARD`, which is `user_grant` with
`available_level = system_basic` and cannot be obtained with a normal
signature; declaring it in `module.json5` makes installation fail with
`code:9568289`. HarmonyOS → Windows clipboard transfer would require the user to
manually press the system `PasteButton`.

Injection authorization dialogs cannot be shown while the device is locked. Only
PC / 2in1 device forms are supported (other forms return `801` from the injection
API).

